{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuTxdVbxho2zQF1n38Eh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard or check that the rule runs, so I haven't seen any panel data or alerts yet.\n\n**Data:** The logs data view has these main fields:\n- `timestamp`\n- `response` (a string, so I used `response.keyword`)\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `clientip`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `machine.os`\n- `host`\n- `url`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-371c8b39 Web logs overview\" has four panels. They show total requests, requests over time, responses by status code, and average bytes by file extension. The link is http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-371c8b39-web-logs-overview-baf7b70cc342.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-371c8b39 5xx spike\" (id `d5008abb-4643-4fec-8dc0-2269bc97add4`) checks every minute. It fires when more than 10 documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` have a `response.keyword` matching `5xx` within a 5-minute window. The rule is created disabled by default, so I enabled it so it can fire.\n\nThe sample data's timestamps may fall outside the last 5 minutes. If so, the rule won't fire until fresh 5xx traffic arrives."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":966,"cache_read_input_tokens":20322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":966},"output_tokens":442,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0536cbf5-c97a-5467-80bd-e50c5d30a2ce","uuid":"e7d53977-5949-419f-8390-7c7323e1e10c","timestamp":"2026-10-10T23:59:54.379Z","request_id":"req_011CfuTxdHwbUJggpPQq1hvE"}
